"P773976027" "Ancestral Warden"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P711482030" "The warehouse has been breached."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2413326582" "{HeroName}. Today we do battle, and today you will die. It is required for us to continue!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - TsooBoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3557681390" "Defeat the head of the Tsoo Safehouse"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P400716966" "You defeated the Ancestral Warden!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3874573005" "You've found information about Mot from the Tsoo's warehouse!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1094588210" "How did it go, {HeroName}? ... ... <br><br>So... Arachnos is here too with some guy named Scirocco? I think I've heard of him. I've got a bad feeling about what's next if they're here...<br><br>It looks like we know what we're up against now, though. It all makes complete sense! It's no wonder that Mot was awakened. We've had so many wars and crises these past few years alone... the Praetorian invasion probably pushed his powers into overdrive and caused him to wake up!<br><br>That's probably why all of us who were from Dark Astoria started having those dreams... Mot's presence was spilling out of the city and affecting us! So... the absorption... that's it! If the death of someone makes him stronger... and someone who dies in agony is even better... then if he absorbs someone who is evil, or who has given up hope, maybe he continues to absorb their power! Or, maybe, it's really a shot in the dark. I suppose at this point we should try to meet up with Sigil, right?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - KoV 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2719691503" "Welcome, {HeroName}. You're just in time to see the destruction of two oathbreakers, two sinners. The woman could have been left alone, if she did not insist on staying by this man's side.<br><br>They are both guilty of many crimes, but, let us pose the question to you. Shall we take just Kadabra's life and spare the woman? Perhaps you wonder why we ask you. An answer is not needed for that, only for the judgement to pass on them."
// Answer Text :
"P550621607" "Just take Kadabra's Life"
// Answer Text :
"P1881011078" "Neither of them are dying today."
// Answer Text :
"P2306366350" "Kill them both, I don't really care."
// Page TakeSigilWarning Text :
"P843157251" "<color orange>You pause for a moment before answering. If you tell these women to take Kadabra's life, they <i>will</i> do it, but Sigil will be safe.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3831645111" "Take Kadabra's life"
// Answer Text :
"P3439771877" "(Reconsider)"
// Page SavingBoth Text :
"P156407017" "<color orange>You pause for a moment before you say your words and look over the situation. Kadabra Kill and Sigil seem to be in some sort of ritual.<br><br>You size up the situation, seeing that you'll have to defeat all of the Knives of Vengeance if you have any hope of rescuing Sigil and Kadabra Kill. However, knowing how determined the Knives are, they will probably begin their ritual to kill the two while you fight them. You're not too sure how long this would take, but it couldn't be more than a few minutes before the two of them are killed.<br><br>If you could take down all of the Knives of Vengeance in this area before they complete the ritual, you could save Kadabra Kill and Sigil. However, if you can't defeat the Knives, then <i>both</i> Sigil and Kadabra Kill will be killed.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1086169894" "I'm saving them both!"
// Answer Text :
"P4109792781" "(Reconsider your options)"
// Page Power Text :
"P1087646840" "<color orange>A smile creeps along the face of the woman.</color><br><br>Hrm... I suppose that could be arranged, {HeroName}. You would truly just allow both of them to die?"
// Answer Text :
"P3190327907" "It doesn't matter to me."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Sigil 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page SavedBoth Text :
"P2607464752" "You saved us both, {HeroName}. We're in your debt.<br><br>Kadabra and I must leave Dark Astoria, I'm afraid. We caused you so much trouble already. We just simply do not have the power to stand toe to toe with the creatures here.<br><br>We'll never forget your help, {HeroName}, I promise you that."
// Answer Text :
"P1630795615" "No problem."
// Page SavedSigil Text :
"P2550272193" "Kadabra...<br><br>I... I don't believe this. It can't be real!<br><br><i>Why</i>, {HeroName}! Why did you save ME and not my husband?! Why did you choose to leave me behind?!<br><br>I gave my very SOUL for his life! How could you do this to me?! Just... just leave me be. I'm taking his remains and leaving this... this cursed city. We never should have come here to begin with... but something told us... something inside both of us felt that we had to stop it.<br><br>Goodbye, {HeroName}. I hope you and I never meet again."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Heather 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page SavedBoth Text :
"P1811158097" "{HeroName}! I just saw Kadabra Kill and Sigil! Thank goodness you were able to rescue them both. This was a HUGE blow to that monster, Mot! Heck, it even makes <i>me</i> feel better about things!<br><br>While you were gone, I had yet another visitor asking for you. He said that he ran into you in the Tsoo warehouse, a 'Mu' by the name of Mu'Vorkan. He claims that Arachnos is trying to work on finding a solution to the Mot problem and that they would like your help.<br><br>I know Arachnos is a villainous organization, but this seems like the only lead that you've got to work on, {HeroName}. With Kadabra Kill and Sigil gone, I'm all out of ideas. I'm honestly going to try to leave this place myself, once I... take care of one last thing."
// Answer Text :
"P1531012350" "What else can you tell me about Mu'Vorkan?"
// Page SavedSigil Text :
"P367117691" "{HeroName}! I just saw Sigil. She... well, she didn't say anything, but I saw her husband's body. {Hero.type=hero Look, I know you did your best, you're a hero, after all. We can't always win them all, but at least Sigil is alive.|I... well, let's just say I'll keep what I'm thinking to myself.}<br><br>While you were gone, I had yet another visitor asking for you. He said that he ran into you in the Tsoo warehouse, a 'Mu' by the name of Mu'Vorkan. He claims that Arachnos is trying to work on finding a solution to the Mot problem and that they would like your help.<br><br>I know Arachnos is a villainous organization, but this seems like the only lead that you've got to work on, {HeroName}. With Kadabra Kill and Sigil gone, I'm all out of ideas. I'm honestly going to try to leave this place myself, once I... take care of one last thing."
// Page SavedNone Text :
"P241111656" "{HeroName}! I haven't seen Kadabra Kill or Sigil yet. What happened?<br><br>... They didn't make it? No... this is... I don't even know what we should do now. They're dead... and now Mot is more powerful than before, and I'm left with no leads on what to do. There... might be something else, though, someone who can help you out, at least.<br><br>While you were gone, I had yet another visitor asking for you. He said that he ran into you in the Tsoo warehouse, a 'Mu' by the name of Mu'Vorkan. He claims that Arachnos is trying to work on finding a solution to the Mot problem and that they would like your help.<br><br>I know Arachnos is a villainous organization, but this seems like the only lead that you've got to work on, {HeroName}. With Kadabra Kill and Sigil gone, I'm all out of ideas. I'm honestly going to try to leave this place myself, once I... take care of one last thing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3151281621" "Let me see if I can get in touch with Sigil... mmph! Something's not right... Someone's talking to me <i>in my mind</i>! It's... Sigil, I think! Hold on...<br><br>...<br><br>...! {HeroName}, this is bad! Sigil says she's been captured by the Knives of Vengeance! They're keeping her and Kadabra Kill in a sewer system nearby!<br><br>They're putting the two of them on some sort of sick trial that is only going to end in their deaths!"
// AcceptString :
"P3241911797" "And that will only make Mot more powerful."
// SendOffString :
"P4237256135" "Right! If Sigil and Kadabra Kill die now, it'll only make things harder for us to actually fight against Mot!<br><br>Sigil gave me a rough location of where they are. {Hero.type=hero You need to go save them! We need to make a stand here and now against Mot!|I know that you don't normally do this, but you need to save them! Our fight against Mot will only be harder if they're taken away!}"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2628902406" "Save Kadabra Kill and Sigil"
// YoureStillBusyString :
